<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anangapala II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Anangpal Tomar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anangapala II was a king of the Tomara dynasty who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> region in the 11th century. He is credited with founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lal-kot">Lal Kot</a>, the earliest identifiable fortified city of Delhi, and the iron pillar now at the Qutb complex is traditionally linked to him. Much of what is known of him comes from later inscriptions and bardic literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anangapala-ii.jpg" alt="Anangapala II" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roboture · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Round_Bations_of_Rai_Pithora.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
